# Backup + Deploy workflow (TeamSuite only)

This repo is **TeamSuite**. Never backup, commit, or deploy **SportSuite360** from this workspace. Never use `c:\SportSuite360`, `C:\SPORTSUITE360_BACKUP`, or `https://sportsuite360.vercel.app`.

When the user asks to **BACKUP** and **DEPLOY** (any casing / Greek/English mix like «KANE BACKUP KAI DEPLOY»):

1. **Filesystem backup first** — run:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "C:\TeamSuite\scripts\backup-project.ps1"
```

This writes a timestamped ZIP to `C:\TeamSuite_backup\TeamSuite_yyyy-MM-dd_HH-mm-ss.zip` (folder is created if missing). Report the ZIP path to the user.

2. **Update backup inventory** — edit `docs/BACKUP-INVENTORY.md`:
   - Append a new row at the **top** of the «Ιστορικό filesystem ZIP» table with: ZIP filename, date, and a short note of what the code backup covered (the changes being shipped).
   - If this session changed **what any backup type includes** (club/platform/cron/mirror/account/script), also update the main «Είδη backup» table so it stays accurate.

3. **Git backup commit** — stage relevant project changes (including `docs/BACKUP-INVENTORY.md` when updated) and commit with message style:

`Backup: <short summary of what changed>.`

Follow the repo git safety rules (no force push, no amend unless allowed, no secrets).

4. **Deploy** — from `C:\TeamSuite`, with `.vercel` linked to project **teamsuite**:

```powershell
npx vercel --prod --yes
```

Report the production URL: `https://teamsuite-seven.vercel.app`.

Do **not** skip the ZIP step when the user asks for backup + deploy together.

# Backup inventory (always)

Whenever backup behavior changes (even without a full BACKUP + DEPLOY request), update `docs/BACKUP-INVENTORY.md` so the table «Ονομασία backup / Τι ακριβώς περιλαμβάνει» stays the source of truth.
